<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="001" project="spaarke-auth-v4-dataverse-MI">
  <metadata>
    <title>Create the dev deployment slot and assign the UAMI</title>
    <phase>0 Spike</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>STANDARD</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Infrastructure setup; no .cs/.ts changes and no ADR surface.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Mechanical Azure CLI work with an exact recipe.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>medium</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Live Azure mutation on the dev App Service; must be operator-observed.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>none</deps>
    <tags>infra,azure,deploy,auth</tags>
    <estimated-effort>1-2 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Create a deployment slot on the dev BFF App Service and assign it the user-assigned managed identity, so the Phase 0 spike and the Phase 3 flip both have an isolated target. The plan supports slots but none exist.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer with Azure App Service and managed-identity experience. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>
  <goal>A running deployment slot on spaarke-bff-dev carrying mi-bff-api-dev, app settings mirrored, verified reachable and NOT swapped.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>design.md §6 mandates a slot-based rollout. E9 established the plan is P1v3 (not the B1 the IaC declares); PHASE-0-LIVE-VERIFICATION confirmed zero slots exist. The slot is needed for Phase 3 regardless.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/spaarke-auth-v4-dataverse-MI/notes/PHASE-0-LIVE-VERIFICATION.md</file>
      <file role="modify">infrastructure/bicep/stacks/dev.bicepparam</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies><dependency task="none" status="complete">Live prerequisites verified 2026-08-19</dependency></dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: dev App Service spaarke-bff-dev in rg-spaarke-dev ONLY. Do not touch spaarke-bff-prod (Stopped) or any other environment.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: assign the EXISTING UAMI mi-bff-api-dev by RESOURCE ID. Never resolve an identity by name — five UAMIs exist and spaarke-bff-identity is a decoy not attached to the BFF.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: DO NOT swap the slot. Creating and deploying to a slot is safe; swapping is task 032.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Scope: the slot runs user-assigned identity only, matching the production slot. Do not enable a system-assigned identity.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Azure App Service slots, managed identity</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/azure-deployment.md</file>
      <file>docs/guides/auth-deployment-setup.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-auth-v4-dataverse-MI/notes/PHASE-0-LIVE-VERIFICATION.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="prescriptive">
    <step>Confirm current state: az webapp deployment slot list on spaarke-bff-dev (expect empty).</step>
    <step>Create the slot (suggested name: staging).</step>
    <step>Assign the UAMI to the slot by full resource ID.</step>
    <step>Mirror app settings from the production slot, including Graph__ManagedIdentity__Enabled=true.</step>
    <step>Deploy the current branch build to the slot; confirm /healthz responds.</step>
    <step>Record slot name, URL and identity assignment in notes/decisions/.</step>
    <step>Reconcile dev.bicepparam, which declares B1 while live is P1v3 (design §10 item 4).</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>Slot creation fails for a quota or tier reason — STOP and report; do not upgrade the plan unilaterally.</trigger>
    <trigger>Mirroring app settings would copy a secret value into a new location — STOP; the secret surface is being reduced, not expanded.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <outputs>
    <output type="azure-resource">spaarke-bff-dev/slots/staging with mi-bff-api-dev assigned</output>
    <output type="doc">projects/spaarke-auth-v4-dataverse-MI/notes/decisions/001-slot-creation.md</output>
    <output type="modify">infrastructure/bicep/stacks/dev.bicepparam</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion>The slot exists and /healthz returns 200.</criterion>
    <criterion>az webapp identity show on the slot reports UserAssigned only, with mi-bff-api-dev.</criterion>
    <criterion>The slot has NOT been swapped; the production slot is unchanged and still serving.</criterion>
    <criterion>No new secret value was written to any new location.</criterion>
    <criterion>dev.bicepparam declares P1v3.</criterion>
    <criterion>Negative case: the assigned principalId is 9fd47efb-7962-492b-ac44-e5ccd0268ebb and NOT c8cdf6fc-a414-4a5b-981c-006d0d84850f (the spaarke-bff-identity decoy).</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
</task>
